**3. BRAND VOICE ****&**** TONE**

**Tone Descriptors**

• Mission-Driven — Talks about the bigger why: environment, farmers, health ecosystem

• Earnest — Genuinely believes in what it does. No cynicism, no irony.

• Informative — Educates without lecturing. Shares facts, not opinions.

• Warm — Speaks like a trusted brand, not a corporation.

• Grounded — Rooted in Indian food culture, seasonal rhythms, traditional wisdom.

**Words We Use**

Raw / earth-grown / untainted / harvest / farmer-backed / soil-to-pantry / whole / pure / certified / chemical-free / farm-fresh / transparent / FOODCERT-audited / PGS-India / cold-pressed / fair price / unadulterated / farmer-first

**Words We Avoid**

Aggressive claims / trendy buzzwords (biohack, stack) / corporate coldness / Caveman's bold/dark energy / anything that makes organic feel elitist

**Default Language: Hinglish**

Pusht's default caption voice is Hinglish. It feels like home. English works for educational content. Mix both for widest reach.

