**Priority Tier 1 — Post Most Often**

**Organic Millets (12 varieties)**

Highest differentiation. Ancient grain education. Each variety has its own story.

• Browntop Millet ₹267–₹530 — most premium. Rare ancient grain story.

• Foxtail Millet ₹160–₹318 — kangni, traditional Indian grain

• Quinoa ₹182–₹360 — bridges traditional and modern health buyer

• All 12 millets → ancient grain education / millet variety comparison / cooking tutorials

**Cold-Pressed Oils**

High AOV. Strong clean-label story. Cold-pressed = nutrition retained.

• White Sesame Oil ₹640 — Pusht's most premium product. Position as a conscious investment.

• Groundnut Oil ₹499 — traditional Indian kitchen staple, cold-pressed upgrade

• Sunflower Oil ₹395 / Black Mustard Oil ₹380 — everyday cold-pressed switch

• Content angle: "Aapka tel cold-pressed hai? Agar nahi, toh yeh dekhiye."

**Forest Honey ₹450**

New addition. High value. Morning immunity angle. Pairs with tea or warm water ritual.

**Priority Tier 2 — Post Regularly**

**Organic Pulses (8 varieties)**

Volume drivers. Sunday dal tadka angle. Farmer story content. Staple upgrade messaging.

• Content angle: "Ghar ki dal alag kyun lagti thi? Kyunki woh certified organic thi."

**Organic Spices (9 products)**

Recipe content. Clean masala angle. Blend comparison with conventional brands.

• Black Pepper ₹210 / Green Cardamom ₹400 / Clove ₹300 — premium spice heroes

**Priority Tier 3 — Post Occasionally**

**Flours ****&**** Cereals**

Recipe-led content. Roti, dosa, porridge tutorials. Functional nutrition angle.

**Farmer Story Framework**

Inspired by TBOF's "soil-first" storytelling. Every Pusht farmer story should include:

• Real name and region of the farmer

• What they grow and how long they have been organic

• One specific number (price paid vs market price, yield per acre, etc.)

• One human detail — why they chose organic farming

Caption pattern: "[Farmer name] ne [X] saal se chemical-free farming ki hai. Unke khet se aapki kitchen tak — yeh hai Pusht ka vaada."

**The Label Padhega India Angle**

"Ek ingredient: Toor Dal. Yeh hai poori ingredient list." Show the label. One word. That's the product.

